# panel.js (source) → panel.min.js (served)

Delivery model (current): the installer bookmarklet is a `javascript:` URL that
appends a `<script src="…jsdelivr…/panel.min.js?<cachebuster>">` — it loads the
code remotely from jsDelivr's GitHub CDN at click time. There is **no embedded
copy** of the source in `index.html` anymore, and the bookmarklet does **not**
inline the source.

- `panel.js` at repo root — the **commented source of truth**; edit this.
- `panel.min.js` — the **built artifact that is actually served**. Comments +
  whitespace stripped, identifiers/syntax untouched (byte-for-byte semantically
  identical). Generated by `scripts/build-min.js` (`npm run build`).

## Hard rules

1. **Never edit `panel.min.js` by hand.** It is generated. Edit `panel.js`, then
   run `npm run build` to regenerate `panel.min.js` before committing.
2. **Bump `TEP_VERSION` in `panel.js`** for a shipped change
   (`const TEP_VERSION = 'X.YZ';` near the top of the IIFE), rebuild, and update
   the displayed version in `index.html`:
   `<span class="install-version" aria-label="Build">X.YZ</span>`.
   (`mirror.html` shows the build number live — it needs no manual bump.)
3. The build strips comments/whitespace only — keep `minifyIdentifiers` and
   `minifySyntax` OFF in `scripts/build-min.js` so the served code stays
   semantically identical to the source. The leading license/disclaimer `/* */`
   banner is preserved verbatim.

## Ship procedure (every panel.js change that goes live)

1. Edit `panel.js`; bump `TEP_VERSION`; update the version span in `index.html`.
2. `npm run build` (regenerates `panel.min.js`).
3. `node -c panel.js && node -c panel.min.js` (sanity).
4. Commit `panel.js`, `panel.min.js`, and any `index.html`/`mirror.html` changes.
5. Push to `main` (jsDelivr serves `@refs/heads/main`).
6. Flush the CDN so clients get the new build immediately:
   `purge.jsdelivr.net/gh/lucidium2000/TE-Optics@refs/heads/main/panel.min.js`.

## Browser compatibility

The bookmarklet is a tiny `<script src>` loader (not a giant inlined URL), so
the old ~500 KB `javascript:` URL length limit no longer applies. It still only
runs on `app.thousandeyes.com` / `app.thousandeyes.us` (the source redirects
elsewhere). CSP: TE allows the jsDelivr script origin; if that ever changes the
delivery model would need revisiting.
